<!-- ==========================================
     HEADER
=========================================== -->

<div class="header">

    <h1>
        🐍 Python Programming
    </h1>

    <p>
        Learn Python programming for placement exams
    </p>

</div>


<div class="container mt-5 mb-5">


    <!-- ==========================================
         INTRODUCTION
    =========================================== -->

    <h2 class="text-center page-title">

        🐍 Python Programming

    </h2>

    <hr>

    <p>

        Python is a high-level, interpreted programming language
        widely used in software development, data science,
        automation, artificial intelligence, and web development.

        Python is also commonly used in coding rounds and
        placement examinations because of its simple syntax
        and powerful built-in features.

    </p>


    <!-- ==========================================
         TOPICS COVERED
    =========================================== -->

    <h4 class="mt-4">

        📚 Topics Covered

    </h4>


    <ul class="list-group mb-4">

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Python Basics
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Variables and Data Types
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Operators
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Conditional Statements
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Loops
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Strings
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Lists
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Tuples and Sets
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Dictionaries
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Functions
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Object-Oriented Programming
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Exception Handling
        </li>

    </ul>


    <!-- ==========================================
         PYTHON TOPICS
    =========================================== -->

    <h4>

        📖 Python Topics and Examples

    </h4>


    <div class="accordion"
         id="pythonTopics">


        <!-- BASIC PYTHON -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#basicPython">

                    1. Basic Python Program

                </button>

            </h2>

            <div
                id="basicPython"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    A simple Python program can use the
                    <strong>print()</strong> function to display
                    output.

<pre>
print("Hello World")
</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- VARIABLES -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#variables">

                    2. Variables and Data Types

                </button>

            </h2>

            <div
                id="variables"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Python variables do not require explicit
                    declaration of their data type.

<pre>
age = 20
marks = 85.5
name = "Manjiri"
grade = 'A'
is_passed = True

print(age)
print(marks)
print(name)
</pre>

                    Common data types include:

                    <ul>

                        <li>int – Integer values</li>

                        <li>float – Decimal values</li>

                        <li>str – Text values</li>

                        <li>bool – True or False</li>

                        <li>list – Collection of values</li>

                    </ul>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- OPERATORS -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#operators">

                    3. Operators

                </button>

            </h2>

            <div
                id="operators"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Operators are used to perform calculations
                    and comparisons.

<pre>
a = 10
b = 3

print(a + b)
print(a - b)
print(a * b)
print(a / b)
print(a % b)
print(a ** b)
</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- IF ELSE -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#ifelse">

                    4. If-Else

                </button>

            </h2>

            <div
                id="ifelse"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Conditional statements are used to execute
                    different blocks of code based on conditions.

<pre>
age = 20

if age >= 18:
    print("Eligible")
else:
    print("Not Eligible")
</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- FOR LOOP -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#forloop">

                    5. For Loop

                </button>

            </h2>

            <div
                id="forloop"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    A for loop is used to repeat a block of
                    code for each item in a sequence.

<pre>
for i in range(1, 6):
    print(i)
</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- WHILE LOOP -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#whileloop">

                    6. While Loop

                </button>

            </h2>

            <div
                id="whileloop"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

<pre>
i = 1

while i <= 5:
    print(i)
    i += 1
</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- STRING -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#strings">

                    7. Strings

                </button>

            </h2>

            <div
                id="strings"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Strings are sequences of characters.

<pre>
name = "Python"

print(name)
print(name[0])
print(name.upper())
print(name.lower())
print(len(name))
</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- LIST -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#lists">

                    8. Lists

                </button>

            </h2>

            <div
                id="lists"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Lists store multiple values in a single
                    variable.

<pre>
numbers = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]

print(numbers)
print(numbers[0])

numbers.append(60)

print(numbers)
</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- DICTIONARY -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#dictionary">

                    9. Dictionary

                </button>

            </h2>

            <div
                id="dictionary"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Dictionaries store data in
                    <strong>key-value pairs</strong>.

<pre>
student = {
    "name": "Rahul",
    "age": 20,
    "branch": "CSE"
}

print(student["name"])
print(student["age"])
</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- FUNCTION -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#functions">

                    10. Functions

                </button>

            </h2>

            <div
                id="functions"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Functions are reusable blocks of code.

<pre>
def add(a, b):
    return a + b

result = add(10, 20)

print(result)
</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- OOP -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#oop">

                    11. Object-Oriented Programming

                </button>

            </h2>

            <div
                id="oop"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Python supports object-oriented programming
                    using classes and objects.

<pre>
class Student:

    def __init__(self, name):
        self.name = name

    def display(self):
        print(self.name)


student = Student("Rahul")

student.display()
</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- EXCEPTION -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#exception">

                    12. Exception Handling

                </button>

            </h2>

            <div
                id="exception"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Exception handling is used to handle runtime
                    errors without stopping the program.

<pre>
try:

    a = 10 / 0

except ZeroDivisionError:

    print("Cannot divide by zero")
</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


    </div>


    <!-- ==========================================
         IMPORTANT QUESTIONS
    =========================================== -->

    <div class="card shadow topic-card mt-5">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h3>
                🎯 Important Python Coding Questions
            </h3>

            <ol>

                <li>Reverse a number</li>

